# User-specific twig assets (Blender files + textures). Keep only .gitkeep
# tracked -- these are a user's own working files, and the Grove twigs they
# derive from are licensed commercial content.
#
# Project overrides that the DATASET depends on are the exception and are
# un-ignored individually below. prepare_assets treats this directory as an
# OVERLAY on the Grove source, so an override tracks only the file that
# actually changed, never a copy of the Grove directory.
/data/input/custom_twigs/*
!/data/input/custom_twigs/.gitkeep
# The silver fir foliage size ladder: seven smaller sprays grown in The Grove
# and appended to the twig. They are Grove OUTPUT, like every tree in the
# dataset -- Grove's own shipped spray stays out, in src/the_grove_23/.
# convert-twigs reads every .blend in a twig directory, so these sit beside the
# Grove file rather than being merged into it.
!/data/input/custom_twigs/PacificSilverFirTwig/
!/data/input/custom_twigs/PacificSilverFirTwig/PacificSilverFirVariants.blend

# Grove commercial software (requires separate license from thegrove3d.com)
/src/the_grove_*/

